<mujoco model="graspable_box">
  <!-- A small parcel sized and tuned to be picked up by a parallel gripper.

       The substrate's first prop meant to be grasped. Every other prop in roqsim_assets is welded
       scenery, and the only free body was the conveyor's package, which rides a belt rather than
       being held. Spawn it with `spawn_model: {model: graspable_box, free: true, publish_tf: dynamic}`
       -- `free` adds the <freejoint/>, so this file deliberately declares none and the same prop can
       still be placed as static scenery.

       Grasp dimension is Y, 0.06 m across the jaws. Sized from the MEASURED aperture range of the
       Unitree Dex1, 5.9 mm to 94.9 mm: 60 mm sits mid-range, so the jaws have travel on both sides of
       contact. A 40 mm box was tried first and is a trap -- only 6 mm inside the closed limit, so the
       position servo has almost no room, and any overshoot on closing extrudes the box sideways out of
       the pads instead of gripping it.

       Contact parameters are chosen for holding, not for looking right:
         * A box primitive, not a mesh. MuJoCo collides meshes by convex hull, and a hull's face
           normals near an edge are what make a pinched object squirt out; an exact box does not have
           that problem, and needs no hull computation.
         * condim="4" adds torsional friction about the contact normal. With condim=3 a box held by two
           flat pads is free to spin about the grasp axis under its own weight -- the grasp holds and
           the parcel rotates out of it anyway.
         * friction sliding 1.2 is high for a cardboard-on-rubber pair, which is what the Dex1's pads
           are; the torsional/rolling terms follow the conveyor package's values.
         * solimp/solref soften the contact slightly (0.9 0.95 0.001 / 0.005 1) so the fingers settle
           into a few tenths of a millimetre of penetration instead of chattering against a rigid face.
           A perfectly stiff pinch at 0.002 s timestep bounces.
       See the port log beside the pick world for the grasp measurements these were tuned against. -->
  <default>
    <geom condim="4" friction="1.2 0.005 0.0001" solimp="0.9 0.95 0.001" solref="0.005 1"/>
  </default>

  <asset>
    <material name="graspable_box" rgba="0.76 0.60 0.42 1"/>
  </asset>

  <worldbody>
    <!-- 0.08 x 0.06 x 0.05 m, 0.5 kg. Mass is on the geom so `spawn_model`'s `mass:` override has a
         single value to scale, and light enough that carrying it does not upset a humanoid's balance
         policy (see the G1 port log, A5). -->
    <body name="graspable_box">
      <geom name="graspable_box" type="box" size="0.04 0.03 0.025" mass="0.5"
            material="graspable_box"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
